The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
substr = strnstr(adapter->vpd->buff, "RM", adapter->vpd->len);
if (!substr) {
    dev_info(dev, "No FW level provided by VPD\n");
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the code attempts to find the firmware version information in the VPD buffer using the substring "RM". If this substring is not found (which is the case for older VIOS servers that do not provide the firmware level), the code logs a misleading message indicating that no firmware level is provided, without properly handling the situation by setting a default firmware version.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
dev_info(dev, "Warning - No FW level has been provided in the VPD buffer by the VIOS Server\n");
ptr = strncpy((char *)adapter->fw_version, "N/A", 3 * sizeof(char));
```
Reason:
The fix updates the log message to be more informative and sets the firmware version to "N/A" when the firmware level is not provided. This ensures that the firmware version is explicitly marked as unavailable, preventing misleading output in the ethtool and improving clarity for users.

